### Example 1: Mixed numbers (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
}

### Example 2: Only even numbers
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [2, 4, 6, 8]
}

### Example 3: Only odd numbers
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [1, 3, 5, 7]
}

### Example 4: Empty array (should fail validation)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": []
}

### Example 5: Missing numbers field (should fail validation)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "data": [1, 2, 3]
}

### Example 6: Non-numeric values (should fail validation)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [1, 2, "three", 4]
}

### Example 7: Negative numbers
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [-2, -4, 1, 3]
}

### Example 8: Float numbers
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [2.5, 4.0, 6.0, 7.5]
}

### Example 9: Large numbers
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [1000, 2000, 3000, 4000]
}

### Example 10: With zero
POST http://localhost:8000/api/sum-even
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numbers": [0, 1, 2, 3]
}
